From 88b27e248e35c5d34128a55b5427bdb35138015c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wjxn13 <236573882+wjxn13@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 23:01:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] feat(core): add cross-agent mention gate, agent labels
 and sticky media routing

Problem
-------
The platform fans every inbound message out to *all* projects. With three
agents (Claude Code / DeepSeek Harness / WorkBuddy) behind one Weixin entry, a
message meant for one agent is also injected into the other two: each injection
is a full model call, so "@dsh do X" spends three agents' worth of quota, and
the two agents that were not addressed tend to answer anyway -- from inside the
agent there is no reliable signal that the message was not for it.

Media makes it worse. Weixin cannot carry text and a photo in one message, so
"@dsh" followed by a photo always arrives as two messages. The photo alone
contains no mention token, so it lands on whichever project owns the platform
default. Measured on this machine (2026-09-19):

  * the photo preview screen has no text box at all;
  * quoting a photo + typing text delivers the text but drops the photo;
  * quoting text + sending a photo delivers the photo but drops the quote.

So no client-side workaround can produce a single message that both names an
agent and carries the image.

Solution
--------
Put an addressing gate inside the engine, ahead of the agent session.

* config: `[[mention_agents]]` declares each project's `aliases`, an optional
  `default` ("answer" / "silent"), and a `media_default` owner. New
  `agent_label` (global, under [display]) and `label` (per project) control the
  outbound identity prefix. `NormalizeMentionAlias` folds case, whitespace and
  a leading `@`, so "@DSH", " @dsh " and "dsh" are the same token.
  `validateMentionAgents` rejects a missing or unknown project, a project
  declared twice, one alias claimed by two projects, an entry with no usable
  alias, and a `default` other than answer/silent.

* engine: `mentionGateBlocked` reads the first @token in the message. Naming a
  peer project drops the message right there -- no session, no agent process,
  no tokens. Naming self, or naming nobody, passes through.

* engine: an unaddressed message still refreshes a short-lived sticky addressee
  (`mention_sticky.go`, TTL 3 min), so a photo sent right after "@dsh" routes to
  dsh instead of the platform default. Sticky state is consulted only for
  messages that carry no text, and it is consumed by the media router rather
  than by the gate, so it cannot reshape text routing. The TTL is short on
  purpose: long enough to cover "type the alias, then pick a photo", short
  enough that someone who walked away does not silently route a much later
  photo to a project they forgot they addressed.

* webhook: `executePrompt` runs the same gate first. A webhook injects a
  synthetic message straight into the processing loop and would otherwise
  bypass the check that `handleMessage` performs.

* ui: `stampAgentLabel` prepends the project's label at the engine's two send
  choke points, so a reply, an error or a queue notice is attributable when
  several projects share one account. The queued-message notice now also states
  the queue position, which agent is holding the session and which one will run
  it, plus how to redirect the message to a peer instead of waiting
  (`MsgMessageQueuedDetail`, `MsgMessageQueuedReroute`); the session-start
  failure notice names the project that failed and offers the recovery path
  (`MsgFailedToStartSessionWhom`). All three keys ship in the five languages the
  rest of the file carries.

Evidence
--------
Live three-agent bridge, 2026-09-19 22:03, after "@dsh" followed by a photo:

  mention gate: media message kept    project=my-dsh        owner=my-dsh
  mention gate: media message dropped project=my-workbuddy token=(media)
  mention gate: media message dropped project=my-project   token=(media)

Text messages in the same batch routed normally, i.e. the sticky addressee did
not leak into text. Compiles clean (`go build ./core/ ./config/ ./cmd/cc-connect/`).
